#: README.md:61
msgid "Theory"
msgstr "理論"

#: README.md:63
msgid "Collective Variables"
msgstr "Collective Variables"

#: README.md:65
msgid ""
"In most of cases, it is impossible to extract clear information about a "
"system of interest by monitoring the cartesian coordinates of all atoms "
"directly, even more if our system contains many atoms. Instead, it is "
"possible to make the monitoring simpler by defining functions of those "
"coordinates that describe the chemical properties that we are interested in."
" Those functions are called Collective Variables (CVs) and allow biasing "
"specific degrees of freedom or analyzing how those properties evolve. Plumed"
" has numerous CVs already implemented that can be used with ASE. For a "
"complete explanation of CVs implemented in Plumed, [go to this "
"link](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html)."
msgstr ""
"全原子の Cartesian "
"座標を直接監視して明確な情報を得るのは、特に大きな系では困難です。対象の化学的性質を記述する座標の関数、Collective Variables "
"(CVs) を定義すれば、特定自由度への Bias や時間変化の解析が容易になります。PLUMED の多数の CV を ASE "
"で使えます。[一覧](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html) "
"を参照してください。"

#: README.md:76
msgid "Metadynamics"
msgstr "Metadynamics"

#: README.md:78
msgid ""
"[Metadynamics](https://www.nature.com/articles/s42254-020-0153-0) is an "
"enhanced sampling method that allows exploring the configuration landscape "
"by adding cumulative bias in terms of some CVs. This bias is added each "
"$\\tau$ time lapse and usually its shape is Gaussian. In time t, the "
"accumulated bias is defined as"
msgstr ""
"[Metadynamics](https://www.nature.com/articles/s42254-020-0153-0) は、CV "
"の関数として Bias を蓄積し地形を探索する Enhanced Sampling 法です。通常 Gaussian を $\\tau$ ごとに加え、時刻"
" t の蓄積 Bias は、"

#: README.md:96
msgid ""
"where $\\mathbf{s}$ is a set of collective variables, $\\sigma_i$ is the "
"width of the Gaussian related with the i-th collective variable, and *W(s, "
"t')* is the height of the Gaussian in time *t'*. In simple metadynamics, "
"*W(s, t')* is a constant, but in Well-Tempered Metadynamics, the height of "
"the Gaussians is lower where previous bias was added. This reduction of "
"height of the new Gaussians decreases the error and avoids exploration "
"towards high free energy states that are thermodynamically irrelevant. The "
"height in time t' for Well-Tempered Metadynamics is"
msgstr ""
"$\\mathbf{s}$ は CV 集合、$\\sigma_i$ は i 番目の Gaussian 幅、*W(s, t')* は時刻 *t'* "
"の高さです。通常は *W(s, t')* 一定ですが、Well-Tempered では既存 Bias "
"のある場所で低くします。誤差を減らし、熱力学的に重要でない高自由エネルギー状態の探索を避けます。時刻 t' の高さは、"

#: README.md:114
msgid ""
"with $W$ the maximum height of the Gaussians, $\\beta$ the inverse of the "
"thermal energy ($1/k_BT$) and $\\gamma$ a bias factor greater than one that "
"regulates how fast the height of the bias decreases: the higher the bias "
"factor, the slower is the decreasing of the heights. Note that when "
"$\\gamma$ approaches infinity, this equation becomes constant and simple "
"metadynamics is recovered. On contrast, when $\\gamma$ approaches zero, no "
"bias is added, which is the case of Molecular Dynamics."
msgstr ""
"$W$ は最大高さ、$\\beta$ は熱エネルギーの逆数 ($1/k_BT$)、$\\gamma$ は1超の Bias Factor "
"です。大きいほど高さがゆっくり減ります。$\\gamma$ が無限大なら一定になり通常 Metadynamics に戻ります。一方 $\\gamma$ "
"が0に近づくと Bias がなく、通常 MD になります。"

#: README.md:122
msgid ""
"The addition of the bias potential produces an extra force in each atom, "
"such that the resultant force for the i-th atom is"
msgstr "BiasPotential により各原子に追加の力が働き、i 番目の合力は、"

#: README.md:134
msgid ""
"where ${\\bf F}_i$ is the natural unbiased force, $R_i$ is the coordinate of"
" the atom, and the second term is the additional force due to the added "
"bias."
msgstr "${\\bf F}_i$ は Unbiased な力、$R_i$ は座標、第2項が Bias による追加の力です。"

#: README.md:137
msgid ""
"Part of the power of metadynamics is that it can be used for exploring "
"conformations. Moreover, the accumulated bias converges to the free energy "
"surface ($F({\\bf s})$),"
msgstr "Conformation 探索に加え、蓄積 Bias から自由エネルギー表面 ($F({\\bf s})$) への収束関係を得られます。"

#: README.md:149
msgid "Planar 7-Atoms Cluster"
msgstr "平面7原子 Cluster"

#: README.md:151
msgid ""
"Let's consider a simple system formed by seven atoms with Lennard-Jones (LJ)"
" interactions in a planar space. This simple model is presented in the "
"[Plumed Masterclass 21.2](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-2.html#masterclass-21-2-ex-9). This LJ cluster has "
"several stable isomers (Figure 1), which can be distinguished in a space of "
"the CVs second (SCM) and third (TCM) central moments of the distribution of "
"coordinations (orange stars in Figure 2)."
msgstr ""
"平面の7 Lennard-Jones (LJ) 原子を考えます。[PLUMED Masterclass "
"21.2](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-2.html#masterclass-21-2-ex-9) のモデルです。複数の安定 "
"Isomer（図1）があり、Coordination Number 分布の SCM・TCM で区別できます（図2の橙の星）。"

#: README.md:162
msgid ""
"**Figure 1.** Local minima isomers of the LJ cluster used in this tutotrial."
msgstr "**図1。** 使用する LJ Cluster の局所極小 Isomer。"

#: README.md:164
msgid ""
"The n-th central moment, $\\mu_n$, of the coordination number of an N-atoms "
"cluster is defined as"
msgstr "N 原子 Cluster の Coordination Number の n 次 Central Moment $\\mu_n$ は、"

#: README.md:175
msgid ""
"where $\\left< {X} \\right>$ is the mean value of $X_i$, which is the "
"coordination of the i-th atom,"
msgstr "$\\left< {X} \\right>$ は i 番目の Coordination $X_i$ の平均です。"

#: README.md:185
msgid ""
"with $r_{ij}$ the distance between atoms $i$ and $j$, and $d$ a reference "
"parameter. For this example, d is fixed to 1.5 $\\sigma$, in LJ units."
msgstr "$r_{ij}$ は原子 $i$・$j$ 間距離、$d$ は参照値です。ここでは LJ 単位で1.5 $\\sigma$ に固定します。"

#: README.md:188
msgid "Molecular Dynamics Simulation"
msgstr "Molecular Dynamics シミュレーション"

#: README.md:190
msgid ""
"For showing that is necessary to use an enhanced sampling method, let's "
"start with a Langevin simulation without bias. In LJ dimensionless reduced "
"units (assuming $\\epsilon$ = 1 eV, $\\sigma$ = 1 $\\textrm Å$ and m = 1 "
"a.m.u), the parameters of the simulation are $k_\\text{B}T=0.1$, friction "
"coefficient fixed equal to 1 and a time step of 0.005."
msgstr ""
"Enhanced Sampling の必要性を示すため、まず Bias なし Langevin MD を行います。LJ 単位（$\\epsilon$ ="
" 1 eV、$\\sigma$ = 1 $\\textrm Å$、m = 1 a.m.u）で、$k_\\text{B}T=0.1$、Friction "
"Coefficient は1、Time Step は0.005です。"

#: README.md:196
msgid ""
"It is supposed that the system should explore all the space of "
"configurations due to thermal fluctuations. However, we can see that the "
"system remains in the same state, even when we sample for a long time lapse."
" That is because a complete exploration of the configuration space could "
"take more time than the possible to simulate. Figure 2 -blue dots- shows the"
" trajectory obtained from the following unbiased Molecular dynamics script "
"[`MD.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/MD.py):"
msgstr ""
"熱揺らぎで全空間を探索するはずですが、長時間でも同状態に留まります。全探索に実行可能な時間以上を要するためです。図2の青点は次の "
"[`MD.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/MD.py) の Trajectory です。"

#: README.md:241
msgid ""
"This simulation starts from the configuration of minimum energy, whose "
"coordinates are imported from "
"[`isomer.xyz`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/isomer.xyz). As you can see in Figure 2, "
"the system remains moving around that state; it does not jump to the other "
"isomers. This means we do not obtain a complete sampling of possible "
"configurations as mentioned before. Then, it is necessary to use an enhanced"
" sampling method as an alternative to observe transitions to other "
"configurations. In this tutorial, we implement Well-Tempered Metadynamics."
msgstr ""
"[`isomer.xyz`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/isomer.xyz) "
"のエネルギー極小から始めます。図2のように同じ状態付近に留まり、別 Isomer への遷移がなく十分 Sampling "
"できません。別構造への遷移を観測するため、Well-Tempered Metadynamics を使います。"

#: README.md:250
msgid ""
"**NOTE** If you want to use a set up from a typical plumed file "
"([`plumedLJ.dat`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/plumedLJ.dat), for this example) to set up"
" the plumed actions, you can replace the `setup` variable assignament in the"
" previous code for:"
msgstr ""
"**注：** 通常の入力（この例なら [`plumedLJ.dat`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/plumedLJ.dat)）を読むには、前の `setup` "
"の代入を次に変えられます。"

#: README.md:259
msgid ""
"Note that in the plumed set-up, there is a line with the keyword UNITS, "
"which is necessary because all parameters in the plumed set-up and output "
"files are assumed to be in plumed internal units. Then, this line is "
"important to mantain the units of all plumed parameters and outputs in ASE "
"units. You can ignore this line if you are aware of the units conversion."
msgstr ""
"UNITS の行で単位を合わせます。PLUMED のパラメータ・出力は内部単位なので、ASE 単位の維持に重要です。変換を理解していれば省略できます。"

#: README.md:262
msgid "Post Processing Analysis"
msgstr "後処理解析"

#: README.md:264
msgid ""
"If you have the trajectory of an MD simulation and you want to compute a set"
" of CVs of that trajectory, you can reconstruct the plumed files without "
"running again all the simulation. As an example, let's use the trajectory "
"created in the last code for rewriting the COLVAR file with the code "
"[`postpro.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/postpro.py):"
msgstr ""
"既存 MD Trajectory の CV は、MD を再実行せず PLUMED 出力を再作成できます。先ほどの Trajectory から "
"[`postpro.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/postpro.py) で COLVAR を作り直します。"

#: README.md:297
msgid ""
"This code, as well as the previous one, generates a file called COLVAR with "
"the value of the CVs. All plumed files begin with a head that describes the "
"fields that it contains. In this case, the heading looks like:"
msgstr "前のコードと同様、CV を含む COLVAR を生成します。PLUMED 出力の先頭には列を説明する Header があり、今回は、"

#: README.md:307
msgid ""
"As you can see, the first column corresponds to the time, the second one is "
"the second central moment (SCM) and the third column is the third central "
"moment (TCM). When we plot this trajectory in the space of this CVs (that "
"is, the second and third columns) we obtain this result:"
msgstr ""
"第1列は時間、第2列は Second Central Moment (SCM)、第3列は Third Central Moment (TCM) "
"です。第2・3列の CV 空間に描くと、"

#: README.md:316
msgid ""
"**Figure 2.** Unbiased MD trajectory (blue dots) in the space of the "
"collective variables second and third central moment. Orange stars represent"
" the location of the local minima isomers of the LJ cluster in this space."
msgstr "**図2。** SCM・TCM 空間の Unbiased MD（青点）。橙の星は LJ Cluster の局所極小 Isomer です。"

#: README.md:320
msgid ""
"Note that the system remains confined in the same stable state. That means, "
"for this case, MD is not enough for exploring all possible configurations "
"and obtaining a statistical study of the possible configurations of the "
"system -at least in the simulated time scale-. Therefore, an alternative is "
"to use an enhanced sampling method. In this case, we implement Well-Tempered"
" Metadynamics for reconstructing the Free Energy Surface (FES)."
msgstr ""
"同じ安定状態に留まるため、少なくともこの時間では MD だけで全 Configuration を探索して統計的に調べられません。Well-"
"Tempered Metadynamics で FES を再構成します。"

#: README.md:327
msgid "Well-Tempered Metadynamics Simulation"
msgstr "Well-Tempered Metadynamics シミュレーション"

#: README.md:329
msgid ""
"Well-Tempered Metadynamics method is described in the [`Theory "
"section`](#metadynamics). It basically adds external energy for pushing the "
"system to explore different conformations. This makes necessary to add a "
"restrain to avoid that the extra energy dissolves the atoms in vacuum. This "
"restriction consists in a semi-harmonic potential with the form"
msgstr ""
"[`Theory section`](#metadynamics) の Well-Tempered Metadynamics は外部エネルギーで別 "
"Conformation を探索させます。真空中で原子が離れるのを防ぐため、次の Semiharmonic Restraint を加えます。"

#: README.md:344
msgid ""
"where $k$ is a constraint, in this case being 1000; $r_w$ is the location of"
" the constraint, that we choose to be 2 (in LJ dimensionless reduced units);"
" $d_i$ is the distance of each atom to the center of mass. Note that this "
"potential does not do anything whereas the distance between the atom and the"
" center of mass is lower than $r_w$, but if it is greater (trying to "
"escape), this potential begins to work and send it back to be close the "
"other atoms. This is defined with the keyword UPPER_WALLS in the plumed set "
"up."
msgstr ""
"$k$ は1000、$r_w$ は LJ 単位で2、$d_i$ は Center of Mass との距離です。$r_w$ "
"未満では作用せず、超えると原子を引き戻します。UPPER_WALLS で定義します。"

#: README.md:353
msgid ""
"Well-Tempered Metadynamics simulation for this case can be run using the "
"code [`MTD.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/MTD.py):"
msgstr ""
"[`MTD.py`](https://github.com/Sucerquia/ASE-"
"PLUMED_tutorial/blob/master/files/MTD.py) で実行できます。"

#: README.md:406
msgid ""
"Note that Well-Tempered Metadynamics requires the value of the temperature "
"according to [equation (2)](#hills) . Then, it is necessary to define the kT"
" argument of the calculator. SIGMA and PACE are the standard deviation of "
"the Gaussians and the deposition interval in terms of number of steps "
"($\\tau$ in [equation (1)](#bias)). HEIGHT and BIASFACTOR are the maximum "
"height of the Gaussians (W) and the $\\gamma$ factor of [equation "
"(2)](#hills), respectively."
msgstr ""
"[式(2)](#hills) の温度として Calculator の kT が必要です。SIGMA は Gaussian 標準偏差、PACE "
"は追加間隔（[式(1)](#bias) の $\\tau$）、HEIGHT は最大高さ W、BIASFACTOR は [式(2)](#hills) の "
"$\\gamma$ です。"

#: README.md:414
msgid ""
"In this case, the Lennard-Jones calculator computes the forces between "
"atoms, namely, ${\\bf F}_i$ forces in [equation (3)](#force). Likewise, you "
"could use your preferred ASE calculator instead of the LJ calculator used "
"here."
msgstr ""
"LJ Calculator が [式(3)](#force) の ${\\bf F}_i$ を計算します。任意の ASE Calculator "
"に変更できます。"

